{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And to Adam He said, etc.</b> One must know for what matter HaShem was particular about his listening to the voice of his wife — He should have said to him nothing but ״כִּי אָכַלְתָּ מִן הָעֵץ״ and so forth? Further, why did He specify saying <b>לְקוֹל אִשְׁתֶּךָ</b>? Further, one must understand His saying the word <b>לֵאמֹר</b>. However, according to what we have explained — that Adam did not know at the time he ate that it was the Tree of Knowledge — it would not be justified to say to him ״כִּי אָכַלְתָּ מִן הָעֵץ״ and so forth, for he did not eat from the tree with knowledge but unwittingly. Therefore HaShem said to him <b>כִּי שָׁמַעְתָּ</b> and so forth — meaning that he accepted his wife's words and did not investigate after her, and from this he was drawn to eat from the tree. And He specified saying <b>לְקוֹל</b> to hint that he did not scrutinize her words, but rather at the mere sound of the words she spoke to him — ״Take and eat״ — he ate, when he should have asked from which tree she had taken [it]. And His saying <b>וַתֹּאכַל מִן הָעֵץ אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ לֵאמֹר</b> — here He alluded to the sin in which he erred unwittingly, for He had commanded him to say to the woman that she should not eat from the tree, and He said ״הָעֵץ אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ לֵאמֹר״ — meaning, to say to the woman, and he did not say to the woman except [concerning] the fruit, as we have scrutinized her words." "And His saying <b>אֲרוּרָה הָאֲדָמָה</b> — and He did not curse Adam as He cursed Eve, for the reason stated in His words, as we have written. And He cursed the earth because it was the cause, for even though Adam commanded the woman only concerning the fruit and not concerning the tree, despite this there would have been no stumbling in this had there not been the change that the earth made in the Tree of Knowledge. Had its tree been like the rest of the trees of the garden, it would not have been a cause for sin, as we have written above. Also, if [the earth] had made all the trees of the garden taste like the tree [tastes] like the taste of the fruit, Adam would have been careful to say to Eve that he was commanded also concerning the tree, and she too would not have laid hand on the tree beforehand. Nor would she have become inflated by it when it changed the taste of the tree from the rest of the trees of the garden. Therefore HaShem cursed the earth, for it was the cause of everything, in that it produced a kind of curse. And Adam He did not curse, but rather by means of this curse HaShem repaid him measure for measure: he listened to his wife and fulfilled his desire in craving to eat a forbidden thing — accordingly, he too [would be] continually בְּעִצָּבוֹן (in pain) and so forth, and it would sprout thorns for him and so forth. And corresponding to the pleasantness of the eating, He said to him <b>וְאָכַלְתָּ אֶת עֵשֶׂב הַשָּׂדֶה</b>. And corresponding to the fact that he did not trouble to know whence the food had come to him, He said <b>בְּזֵעַת אַפֶּיךָ</b> and so forth — that he would not obtain food in tranquility without toil."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:58.627306244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}